            <ArticleTitle>[Negativity of the exercise thallium test despite tight stenosis of the common trunk of the left coronary artery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>211-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a case of severe angina linked to subocclusive ostial stenosis of the common trunk of the left coronary, characterised by the contrast between a very positive stress test on the basis of clinical and electrocardiographic parameters and a negative Thallium stress test. The occasion is taken to review the sensitivity of Thallium stress testing in lesions of the common trunk.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
